Falsifies `usb::verification::the_descriptor_walk_is_total_and_yields_whole_descriptors`.

The defect: the walk checks only that a descriptor holds its own length and type, and no longer
that an interface or endpoint descriptor holds its fixed layout. A two-byte endpoint descriptor is
then yielded whole by its own length, and a caller that indexes it by the endpoint layout reads
past its end, into the next descriptor or out of the buffer.

Expected to fail: the harness's "it holds its fixed layout" assertion.

diff --git a/src/descriptor.rs b/src/descriptor.rs
--- a/src/descriptor.rs
+++ b/src/descriptor.rs
@@ -427,9 +427,6 @@
             ENDPOINT => ENDPOINT_DESCRIPTOR_BYTES,
             _ => 2,
         };
-        if len < layout {
-            return self.malformed(at);
-        }
         self.at = at + len;
         Some(Ok(&configuration[at..at + len]))
     }
